      "title": "Absolute assignment transfers ownership rights",
      "narration": "Suppose Elena executes a valid absolute assignment to her adult daughter. An absolute assignment transfers the ownership rights described by that complete transfer. The daughter becomes the new owner through the required process. This is different from naming her beneficiary, which only addresses who receives an applicable benefit. Changing ownership does not ordinarily change the person whose life is insured. It also does not erase existing policy limitations, loans or superior interests. The parties should review the actual assignment and obtain any required consent or recording. A transfer can have tax consequences that deserve separate review.",
